hadiths[count]{hadithnumber,text}:
"7800","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Muhammad bin Sinan Al-Qazzaz told us, Abdullah bin Hamran told us, Abd al-Hamid bin Jaafar told us, Abdullah bin Tha'labah, that he came to Abd al-Rahman bin Ka'b bin Malik, and he was wearing a stripped garment, and he went around behind the house, trying to hide it. While he was being led blind, he said: I greeted him, and he said: Who is this? I said: Abdullah bin Tha'labah. He said: Brother of Banu Harithah? I said: Yes, and Juhayna’s circumcision? I said: Yes. He said: Did you hear your father narrating a hadith that you heard him narrating on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace? He said: I do not know. He said: I heard your father saying: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: “Whoever seizes the property of a Muslim by swearing an oath... A lie, it was a black mark in his heart that nothing will change until the Day of Resurrection.” This hadith has an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it with this. “They only agreed on the hadith of Al-A’mash and Mansour, on the authority of Abu Wa’il, on the authority of Abdullah, with his wording.”\n[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7800 - True"
"7801","Ahmad bin Kamil Al-Qadi told us, Muhammad bin Saad Al-Awfi told us, Ruh bin Ubadah told us, Shu’bah told us, he said: I heard Ayadh Abu Khalid, He says: I saw two men disputing at Maqil bin Yasar, and Maqil said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, say: “Whoever swears an oath To take with it the wealth of a man who met God Almighty while angry with Him. This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration. They did not narrate it with this chain of narration.\n[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7801 - True"
"7802","Ahmad bin Kamil told us, Ahmad bin Ubayd Allah bin Idris told us, Yazid bin Harun told us, Hisham bin Hassan told us, on the authority of Muhammad Ibn Sirin, on the authority of Imran Ibn Husayn, may God be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Whoever swears a false oath Let him take his seat in the Fire.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs, and they did not narrate it with this wording.\n[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7802 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"7803","Muhammad ibn Salih ibn Hani told me, Abu Sa`id al-Hasan ibn Abd al-Samad al-Qundazi told me, Yahya ibn Yahya told me, and Amr ibn Zurarah, they said: Saeed bin Salamah told us, Ismail bin Umayyah told us, on the authority of Omar bin Ata bin Abi Al-Hawar, on the authority of Ubaid bin Jurayj, on the authority of Al-Harith bin Al-Barsa, may God be pleased with him, said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, during Hajj between the two Jamarats, saying: “Whoever cuts If his Muslim brother inclines to take an immoral oath, let him take his seat in the Fire, so that your witness may convey to your absent witness” two or three times. This is an authentic hadith. The chain of transmission and they did not produce it in this context.”\n[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7803 - True"
"7804","Abu Ishaq Ibrahim bin Ismail Al-Qaari told us, Othman bin Saeed Al-Darimi told us, Saeed bin Abi Maryam told us, Nafi bin Yazid Al-Masri, Abu Sufyan bin Jabir bin Atik narrated to me, on the authority of his father, may God be pleased with him, that he heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. He says: “Whoever seizes the wealth of a Muslim by swearing an oath, God will forbid him Paradise and admit him to Hell.” They said: O Messenger of God, even if it is a small thing? He said: “Even if it is a siwak, even if it is a siwak.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it in this context.\n[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7804 - True"
"7805","Abu Bakr Ismail bin Muhammad al-Faqih told us about Rayy, Sa`id bin Yazid told us, on the authority of Atiya, Waki` bin al-Jarrah told us, Al-Harith told us Ibn Sulaiman Al-Jundi, on the authority of Kurdous Al-Thaalabi, on the authority of Al-Ash’ath ibn Qays, may God be pleased with him, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, that he said: “Who He swore an oath by which the property of a Muslim man would be taken away while he was an immoral person and met God while he was a leper. This hadith has an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it. \"With this increase\"\n[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7805 - True"
"7806","Al-Hasan bin Yaqoub Al-Adl told us, Yahya bin Abi Talib told us, Abdul Wahhab bin Ata told us, Abdullah bin Aoun informed us, On the authority of Al-Sha’bi, on the authority of Al-Ash’ath ibn Qays, may God be pleased with him, that he disputed with a man before the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, in a land, so he made an oath on One of them, and the other said: O Messenger of God, if he swears, I will give him my land. Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Leave him, for he is the one who swore to An oath of patience to take the money of a Muslim man who meets God Almighty on the Day of Resurrection while he is angry with him. May God forgive him or her. “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it in this context.”\n[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7806 - True"
"7807","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Al-Abbas bin Muhammad Al-Duri told us, Uthman bin Omar told us, Ibn Abi Dhib told us, on the authority of Al-Harith Ibn Abd al-Rahman, on the authority of Abu Salamah, said: There was a dispute between Sa`id ibn Zayd and the daughter of Arwa, so Marwan said: Reconcile between these two. So we told him about that until we said, “I will do justice to this woman,” and he said: Do you think I have deprived her of her right in some way, when I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace? He, peace and blessings be upon him, said: “Whoever seizes a span of land, God Almighty will encircle him on the Day of Resurrection from seven lands, and whoever seizes wealth with his oath will not Blessed be he for it, and whoever takes charge of a people without their permission, upon him is the curse of God, the angels, and all mankind.” This hadith has an authentic chain of narration. They did not expel him in this context.”\n[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7807 - True"
"7808","Abdullah bin Al-Hussein Al-Qadi told me, Al-Harith bin Abi Usama told us, Yunus bin Muhammad told us, Al-Layth bin Saad told us, on the authority of Hisham bin Saad, on the authority of Muhammad bin Zayd bin Muhajir, on the authority of Abu Umamah Al-Ansari, on the authority of Abdullah bin Anis Al-Juhani, may God be pleased with him, that The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Among the greatest sins are associating others with God, being disobedient to one’s parents, a false oath, and no one who swears an oath. By God, he took a patient right hand, so he entered into it like the wing of a mosquito, except that God will make it a mark in his heart on the Day of Resurrection.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration. And they did not bring it out.”\n[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7808 - True"
"7809","Abu Bakr bin Ishaq told us, Ismail bin Ishaq told us, Sulaiman bin Harb told us, and Muslim bin Ibrahim told us, they said: Thana Shu’bah, Abu Al-Tayyah told me, on the authority of Abu Al-Aaliyah, on the authority of Abdullah bin Masoud, may God be pleased with him, who said: “We used to count among the sins that were not For him is expiation for a dimpled oath. It was said: What is a dimpled oath? He said: “A man seizes a man’s wealth with his right hand.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs. They did not narrate it, as they agreed on the support of the companion’s statement.\n[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7809 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"7810","Bakr bin Muhammad bin Hamdan Al-Maruzi told us, Abd Al-Samad bin Al-Fadl told us, Makki bin Ibrahim told us, Hashim bin Hashim told us Ibn Utbah, on the authority of Abdullah Ibn Nastas, the client of Kathir Ibn Al-Salt, on the authority of Jabir Ibn Abdullah, may God be pleased with them both, who said: The Messenger of God said God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him: “Whoever swears a sinful oath on my pulpit, let him take his seat in Hell - or he said: unless Hell becomes necessary for him - Even if it was on a green siwak, “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.” It was narrated by Malik bin Anas, on the authority of Hashim bin Hashim\n[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7810 - True"
"7811","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Abdul-Hakam told us, Ibn Wahb told me, Malik bin Anas, on the authority of Hashim bin Hashim bin Utbah bin Abi Waqqas, on the authority of Abdullah bin Nastas, on the authority of Jabir bin Abdullah Al-Sulami, may God be pleased with him On their authority, the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Whoever swears a sinful oath on my pulpit, let him take his seat in Hell.”"
"7812","Abu Al-Hussein Muhammad bin Ahmad Al-Qantari told us, in Baghdad, Abu Qalaba told us, Abu Asim told us, Al-Hasan bin Yazid Al-Dhamri told us, He said: I heard Abu Salama bin Abdul Rahman say: I bear witness that I heard Abu Hurairah, may God be pleased with him, saying: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said And he said: “No male or female slave will swear at this pulpit on a sinful oath, even on a wet siwak, except that Hell will be required for him.” This is a hadith. It is correct according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, because this Hassan bin Yazid is Abu Yunus, the strong and devout, and they did not narrate it.”\n[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7812 - True"
"7813","Abu Abdullah Al-Saffar told us, Ahmad bin Mihran told us, Ubaid Allah bin Musa told us, Israel informed us, on the authority of Muawiyah bin Ishaq, On the authority of Sa’id bin Abi Sa’id al-Maqbari, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, may God be pleased with him, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, who said: “God has given me permission to narrate About a rooster whose feet are on the ground and whose neck is bent under the Throne, and he says: Glory be to You, how great is our Lord. “That is he who swears by me falsely.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.\n[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7813 - True"
"7814","Ali bin Hamshadh Al-Adl told us, Ali bin Al-Hussein bin Al-Junaid told us, Sahl bin Othman Al-Ataki told us, Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, Al-Hasan bin Ubayd Allah Al-Nakhai narrated to us, on the authority of Saad bin Ubaidah, who said: Ibn Umar, may God be pleased with them both, heard a man swearing by the Kaaba and he said: No. Swear by the Kaaba, for I heard the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, say: “Whoever swears by other than God has disbelieved or associated partners.” This is an authentic hadith. According to the conditions of the two sheikhs, and they did not narrate it.”\n[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7814 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"7815","Ali bin Al-Hussein Al-Subaie told us, in Kufa, Ahmed bin Hazim Al-Ghafari told us, Muhammad bin Ubaid Al-Masoudi told us, on the authority of Ma’bad bin Khalid, on the authority of Abdullah bin Yasar, on the authority of Qutaylah bint Saifi, a woman from Juhayna, who said: Habru came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, He said: You associate partners, you say whatever God wills and you will, and you say, “By the Kaaba.” The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Say what God wills, then “Whatever you wish, say, ‘By the Lord of the Kaaba.’” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.\n[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7815 - True"
"7816","Abu Sahl Ahmad ibn Muhammad al-Nahwi told us, in Baghdad, Ja`far ibn Muhammad ibn Shakir told us, Abdullah ibn Dawud told us, Al-Walid told us Ibn Tha'labah Al-Tai, on the authority of Abdullah Ibn Buraydah, on the authority of his father, may God be pleased with him, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “None of us “He swore to be faithful, and he is not one of us who deceives a man’s wife or his slave.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.\n[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7816 - True"
"7817","Ali bin Hamshadh Al-Adl told me, Ismail bin Ishaq Al-Qadi told me, Muslim bin Ibrahim told us, Ubais bin Maimun told us, Yahya bin Abu Kathir, on the authority of Abu Salamah, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, may God be pleased with him, said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Whoever swears an oath is as If he swears that he is a Jew, then he is a Jew, and if he says that he is a Christian, then he is a Christian, and if he says that he is free from Islam, then he is He is innocent of Islam, and whoever claims the claim of pre-Islamic times is one of the people of Hell. They said: O Messenger of God, even if he fasts and prays? He said: “And if he fasts and prays,” this is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.\n[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7817 - The news is objectionable"
"7818","Abu Al-Abbas Qasim bin Al-Qasim Al-Sayyari told us, with Marwa, Ibrahim bin Hilal Al-Jawzjani told us, Ali bin Al-Hassan bin Shaqiq told us, Al-Hussein bin Waqid told us, Abdullah bin Buraidah told us, on the authority of his father, may God be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “Who He said, “I am innocent of Islam. If he is lying, then it is as he said, and if he is truthful, he will never return to Islam unscathed.” This is an authentic hadith. According to the conditions of the two sheikhs, and they did not narrate it.”\n[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7818 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"7819","Muhammad bin Ali Al-Shaybani told us, in Kufa, Ahmad bin Hazim Al-Ghafari told us, Abu Nu’aym and Abu Ghassan told us, they said: A partner told us, On the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Rab’i ibn Harash, Ali ibn Abi Talib narrated to us, may God be pleased with him, who said: When the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, opened Mecca. People from the Quraysh came to him and said: Some of our loyalists and slaves have overtaken you. They have no desire for religion except fleeing from our livestock. And we planted. Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “By God, oh people of Quraysh, you must perform the prayer and pay the zakat, or I will send a man over you who will strike. Your necks on religion.” Then he said: “I am the one who cuts the sandal.” Ali said: “And I am the one who trims the sandal of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace.”\nThen Ali said: I heard the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: “Whoever lies about me will enter Hell.” This is an authentic hadith according to the condition of Muslim, and they did not narrate it.”\n[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7819 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"7820","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Dinar, the ascetic justice, told us, Ahmad bin Muhammad bin Nusayr told us, Abu Nu’aym told us, he told us Ismail bin Qais bin Saad bin Zaid bin Thabit Al-Ansari, my father told me, on the authority of Kharijah bin Zaid, on the authority of Zaid, may God be pleased with him, he said: While the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was sitting with his companions talking to them, he got up and entered, and Zaid arose and sat in the seat of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. And he began to tell them about the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, when he passed meat as a gift to the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, so the people said to Zaid, and it was The most recent of them: O Abu Saeed, if you stood up to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and conveyed our greetings to him and said to him: Your companions will say to you: If... You thought you would send us some of this meat. He said: “Go back to them, for they have eaten meat after you.” Then Zaid came and said: I have conveyed the message to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he said: “Go back to them.” They ate meat after you. The people said: We did not eat meat. This matter happened, so they went with us to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and asked him what this was. They came to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. He greeted them, and they said: O Messenger of God, we sent you the meat that was brought to you. Zaid claimed that they had eaten meat, but by God we did not eat meat. Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “It is as if I were looking at the greenness of the flesh of Zayd in your teeth.” They said: “Messenger of God, so ask forgiveness for us.” He said: So he asked forgiveness for them, “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.”\n[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7820 - Ismail bin Qais bin Saad bin Zaid bin Thabit weak him"
"7821","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Ahmad Al-Mahboubi informed us, Saeed bin Masoud told us, Ubayd Allah bin Musa told us, Israel informed us, about Ibrahim bin Abdul-Ala, on the authority of his grandmother, on the authority of her father, Suwayd bin Hanzala, said: We went out seeking the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and with us. Wael bin Hajar, and an enemy of his took him. The people were embarrassed to swear, and I swore that he was my brother, so let him go. So we came to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. Peace be upon him, so I told him that the people were embarrassed and I swore that he was my brother, so he said: “You have told the truth about the Muslim, the brother of the Muslim.” This is an authentic hadith. The chain of transmission and they did not narrate it.”\n[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7821 - True"
"7822","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Al-Hasan bin Ali bin Affan Al-Amiri told us, Abu Usama told us, Al-Walid bin Kathir told us, he told me Abdul Rahman bin Al Harith, on the authority of Amr bin Shuaib, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abdullah bin Amr, may God be pleased with them, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace He, peace and blessings of God be upon him, said: “Whoever divorces what he does not own, there is no divorce for him. Whoever frees what he does not own, there is no emancipation for him. And whoever makes a vow regarding what he does not own, there is no vow.” And whoever swears to disobey him will not have an oath, and whoever swears to sever ties of family ties will not have an oath.” This hadith has an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it. And from Amr bin Shuaib, there is another chain of narration in it."
"7823","Abu Bakr bin Ishaq told us, Abu Al-Muthanna told us, Musaddad told us, Yazid bin Zurayi told us, Habib bin Al-Muallem told us, on the authority of Amr bin Shuaib, on the authority of Sa`id ibn al-Musayyab, that two Ansar brothers had an inheritance between them, and one of them asked its owner about the division, and he said: If you return You asked me to share, I will never speak to you, and all my money is in the covering of the Kaaba. Omar bin Al-Khattab, may God be pleased with him, said: Indeed, the Kaaba is insufficient. What's wrong with you, make amends for your oath and speak to your brother, for I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: “You shall not swear an oath or vow to disobey the Lord or to “Severing ties of kinship or in what you do not own.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.\n[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7823 - True"
"7824","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Abu Al-Bakhtari Abdullah bin Muhammad bin Shaker told us, Asbat bin Muhammad Al-Qurashi told us, Al-Shaybani, on the authority of Abdul Aziz bin Rafi’, on the authority of Tamim Al-Tai, who said: A man came to Adi bin Hatim, may God be pleased with him, and said: I I married a woman, so give me. He said: I write for you a shield and a shield, and you will give it to them. The man became angry, so Uday swore not to give it to them. The man said: I was hoping that You give me a groomsman. He said: By God, they are more beloved to me than two groomsmen. The man said: Write for me about them. Uday said: I heard the Messenger of God. May God’s prayers and peace be upon him. He said: “If one of you takes an oath and sees something better than it, let him do what is better.” I have not written for you about them. He said: “So he wrote.” “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it in this context.”\n[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7824 - True"
"7825","Muhammad bin Saleh bin Hani told us, Yahya bin Muhammad bin Yahya told us, Al-Hakam bin Musa told us, Al-Haytham bin Humaid told us, on the authority of Zaid Ibn Waqid, on the authority of Bishr ibn Ubayd Allah, on the authority of Ibn Aidh, on the authority of Abu Al-Darda’, may God be pleased with him, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, who said: God has given his Messenger camels, so he dispersed them. Then Abu Musa Al-Ash’ari said: O Messenger of God, carry me. He said: “No.” He said to him three times, and the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “I will not.” He said: There remained four small children, so he said: “O Abu Musa.” Take them.” He said: O Messenger of God, I am ashamed to ask you, but you prevented me and I swore, but I feared that he had entered upon the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. An illusion. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “If I swear and see that something other than that is better, I atone for my oath and do what is better.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs, but they did not narrate it.”\n[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7825 - according to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"7826","Abu Al-Imam told us, Muhammad bin Ishaq and Muhammad bin Nu’aym told us, they said: Abu Al-Ash’ath told us, Muhammad bin Abdul Rahman Al-Taffawi told us, Hisham bin Urwa told us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Aisha, may God be pleased with her, who said: Whenever the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, swore an oath He would not break his oath until God Almighty revealed the expiation for an oath. He said: “I do not swear an oath and see another one that is better than it, unless I atone for one oath and then “I have come to that which is better.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs, but they did not narrate it.\n[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7826 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"7827","Ibrahim bin Ismail Al-Qaari told me, Othman bin Saeed Al-Darimi told us, Yahya bin Saleh Al-Wahazi told us, Muawiyah bin Salam told us, On the authority of Yahya bin Abi Kathir, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, may God be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “Whoever If he takes an oath against his family, it is a greater sin.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Al-Bukhari.\n[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7827 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"7828","Ahmad ibn Ja`far al-Quta’i told us, Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal told us, my father told me, Abd al-Razzaq told us, he informed us Muammar, on the authority of Hammam ibn Munabbih, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, may God be pleased with him, that the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “If one of you “By swearing an oath to his family, then he is a sinner in the sight of God because of the expiation that he was commanded to do.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs, and they did not narrate it.\n[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7828 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"7829","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Muhammad bin Ishaq Al-Saghani told us, Ya’la bin Ubaid told us, Abu Saad Al-Bakqal told us, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, said: A man came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and said: My sister swore that she would walk to house, and that it was difficult for her to walk. He said: “Tell her to ride if she is not able to walk, for God is not sufficient to make it difficult for your sister.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.”\n[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7829 - True"
"7830","Al-Hasan bin Halim told us, Abu Al-Mujih told us, Al-Hussein bin Harith told us, Al-Fadl bin Musa told us, on the authority of Sharik, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, in A man swears to walk, but is unable, so he rides. He said: Ibn Abbas said: “He will perform Hajj from Qabil, and ride as long as he walks, and walk as long as he rides.”\nA partner said: Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman, the client of Talha’s family, narrated to us on the authority of Kurayb, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them, that a man came to The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: My sister has been made obligated to walk to the House of God. He said: “Indeed, God Almighty will not do anything to your sister’s misery.” Say “Let her perform Hajj riding, and let her oath be expiated.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim, but they did not narrate it.\n[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7830 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"7831","Abdullah bin Ja’far bin Darastawayh told us, Ya’qub bin Sufyan told us, Abdul Aziz bin Abdullah Al-Uwaisi told us, Abd told us Al-Rahman bin Abi Al-Rijal, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Amra, on the authority of Aisha, may God be pleased with her, who said: Give me meat as a gift, so the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, commanded me. He, peace be upon him, asked me to give some of it as a gift to Zainab, so I gave it to her and she returned it. He said: “Increase it.” So I increased it and she returned it, so he said: “I swore to you not to “You increased it.” So I increased it, and she returned it, and jealousy came over me, so I said: She insulted you. He said: “You and she are more insignificant to God than to be insulted by you.” Uhud, I swear that I will not enter upon you for a month.” So he was absent from us on the twenty-nine, then he entered upon us on the evening of the thirtieth. She said: I swore that you would not enter. A month, so he said: “A month like this and a month like that,” and he separated his palms and held the thumb in the third place. “This is an authentic hadith on the condition that Al-Bukhari did not narrate it, and it contains the explanation, “I swore an oath and an oath to such and such.”\n[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7831 - According to Al-Bukhari’s condition"
"7832","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Abdul-Hakam told us, Ibn Wahb told us, Amr told us Ibn Al-Harith, that Kathir Ibn Farqad narrated to him, that Nafi’ narrated to them, on the authority of Abdullah Ibn Omar, may God be pleased with them both, on the authority of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. He, peace and blessings of God be upon him, said: “Whoever swears an oath and then says: If God wills, then he will have his second. This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it like this.”\n[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7832 - True"
"7833","Abu Bakr bin Ishaq told us, Al-Hasan bin Ali told us, on the authority of Ibn Ziyad, Manjab bin Al-Harith told us, Ali bin Mushar told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Mujahid, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, said: “If a man takes an oath, he has the right to make an exception, even for a year.” And this verse was revealed regarding this matter: {And remember your Lord when you forget} [Al-Kahf: 24]. He said: “When He is mentioned, he turns away.” Ali bin Mushar said: “And Al-A’mash used to take it.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs, but they did not narrate it.\n[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7833 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"7834","Abu Bakr bin Ishaq told us, Muhammad bin Issa bin Al-Sakan Al-Wasiti told us, Omar bin Aoun told us, Hushaym told us, Abd told us Allah bin Abi Salih, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, may God be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Your oath is upon what confirms you.” With your friend”\n[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7834 - It is true, God willing"
"7835","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Ahmad bin Abdul-Jabbar told us, Abu Muawiyah told us, Bashar bin Kadam Al-Sulami told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Zayd, on the authority of Ibn Omar, may God be pleased with them both, said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “An oath is an oath or one that is regretful.” Al-Hakim said: “The For a while in my life, I thought this Bashar was the brother of Mas’ar, but I did not meet him, and this statement is correct from what Ibn Umar said.”\n[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7835 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"7836","Ahmad bin Sahl Al-Bukhari told us, Sahl bin Al-Mutawakkil told us, Ibrahim bin Al-Mundhir told us, Abu Damrah told us, on the authority of Asim bin Muhammad Ibn Zayd Ibn Abdullah Ibn Omar Ibn Al-Khattab, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Ibn Omar, may God be pleased with them both, who said: “Oaths are only a sin or “Remorse” is the last book of faith.\n[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7836 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
